robopi-analyze (1.0.5-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add thermal dimension: sample CPU/GPU/NPU/package/center thermal zones
    on the same timeline as the other dimensions.
  * Revert dimension 03 to full dmesg history (boot log plus live follow);
    the analyzer already drops events outside the session window by
    default and --keep-outside still recovers the full history.
  * Flush can.asc and the ring pcap into the session directory every
    FLUSH_INTERVAL_SECS (default 10) instead of only at teardown.
  * Translate remaining Chinese comments in the boot-capture hardening
    work to English.

 -- wentywenty <2321901849@qq.com>  Wed, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800

robopi-analyze (1.0.4-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Default the session root to /home/robo/robopi-logs (SESSION_ROOT) and
    preflight free space before starting a capture; the old /var/log/robopi
    default sits on a 47 MB zram and a single session fills it.
  * Add robopi-session-cleanup and run it before each capture: sessions
    older than SESSION_RETENTION_DAYS or beyond SESSION_RETENTION_COUNT are
    removed, the newest one is always kept.
  * Record the board serial number and boot id in manifest.json.
  * Capture CAN traffic on "any" so interfaces that appear late (the
    EtherCANFD can0-can3) are recorded without any wait logic; log2asc
    still converts only can0-can3.
  * Wait for CAN_INTERFACE before resolving usbmon in the ring capture
    instead of aborting when it is absent.
  * Retry attaching the inference screen session instead of checking once
    and giving up silently.
  * Follow the bms.service journal stream and journalctl -k for kernel
    messages instead of truncated status polls and replayed dmesg history.
  * Analyzer: structured BMS events, short-unix dmesg parsing, and can-asc
    filtered to can0-can3 to match the ASC output.

 -- wentywenty <2321901849@qq.com>  Wed, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800

